					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/openai_logo-1.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI's data agent in ChatGPT Work still isn't accurate enough. Under the codename "Athena," the company is building a semantic layer that gives agents standardized definitions for business metrics. The tool could also put OpenAI in direct competition with Snowflake and Databricks.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/openai-is-building-athena-data-platform-to-cut-down-on-ai-agent-guesswork/">OpenAI is building &quot;Athena&quot; data platform to cut down on AI agent guesswork</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
